### 51. Upload a HEIC photo -> 400 Bad Request, whose detail explains it
### An iPhone shoots HEIC by default. The front has to explain this, or convert to JPEG before sending.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/lists/{{photoListId}}/cover
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="photo.heic"
Content-Type: image/heic

< ./photo.heic
--WebAppBoundary--

> {%
    client.test("Returns 400 mentioning HEIC", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 400, "Expected 400 but got " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.detail.indexOf("HEIC") >= 0, "Expected the HEIC hint");
    });
%}

### 52. Upload a file over 8 MB -> 413 Content Too Large
### Answered by the servlet container before any code runs, so even on somebody else's list.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/lists/{{photoListId}}/cover
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="too-big.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./too-big.jpg
--WebAppBoundary--

> {%
    client.test("Returns 413", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 413, "Expected 413 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### 53. Send the file as JSON instead of multipart -> 415 Unsupported Media Type
### It was a 500 before; POST /media answers the same 415 now.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/lists/{{photoListId}}/cover
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "file": "not a file" }

> {%
    client.test("Returns 415", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 415, "Expected 415 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### 54. Exhaust this account's upload allowance -> 429 Too Many Requests with Retry-After
### Not scripted as one request: the allowance is shared with POST /media (20 per 10 minutes by default, admins
### exempt), so run request 44 more than app.media.upload-limit times inside the window - or see media.http request
### 14, which does it with POST /media. The answer carries Retry-After; a request about somebody else's list is a 404
### BEFORE the allowance is looked at, so it never costs an upload.

### 55. Saturate the decode pool -> 503 Service Unavailable with Retry-After
### Not scriptable by hand either: it needs more simultaneous uploads than app.media.max-concurrent-processing.
### Same answer as POST /media (media.http request 13).

